Move complete nominal function lowering into HIA kernels

Implement ordered block admission, operations, terminators, helper requests and
Core function materialization with five explicitly selected HIA owners. Bind
all kernels to the current cold source, source distributions, installed resources
and six mandatory CI modules without fallback or skipped controls.

Close native sessions at the public elaboration boundary, including failed
initialization, while preserving every private elaborator method and partial
state. Retain the original lifetime witness and independent corrected replay.

Preserve exact-source f50 qualification and new source-scoped development
results: 134 public cases, 1,586 mutations, legacy imports, real source-package
installation, 3 lifecycle tests, 33 function tests and 26 final source controls.
Constructor and outer owners remain separate candidates. The final v63 tree
requires its own unchanged 180-second, two-worker cold and full acceptance;
whole-stack closure and legacy-owner retirement are not claimed.